---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Disclaimer', href: '/disclaimer/' },
];

const lastReviewed = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Important disclaimers about this site's independent, informational nature, and the limits of the information published here."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-faint">Last reviewed: {lastReviewed}</p>

      <h2>Independent Information Resource</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.siteName} is an independent website that publishes
        information about the Gold Rummy Android application, including
        download guidance, installation steps, feature explanations and
        promotional information. Unless explicitly stated otherwise on a
        specific page, this site has not confirmed an official affiliation,
        partnership, sponsorship or endorsement relationship with Gold
        Rummy's publisher or developer.
      </p>

      <h2>No Guarantee of Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        We make a genuine effort to keep the information on this site
        accurate and current, including clearly labelling any detail we
        haven't been able to verify as a placeholder rather than presenting
        it as fact. Even so, app details such as version numbers, file
        sizes, features, promotional terms and legal status can change
        without notice on the publisher's side, and this site may not
        reflect a change immediately. Always confirm current details inside
        the official Gold Rummy app before relying on anything published
        here.
      </p>

      <h2>No Financial or Legal Advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site constitutes financial, legal or professional
        advice. Content describing bonuses, promo codes or gameplay formats
        is provided for general informational purposes only and should not
        be treated as a guarantee of any specific outcome, reward or
        legality in your location.
      </p>

      <h2>Financial Risk</h2>
      <p>
        Gold Rummy involves real-money gameplay on at least some tables.
        Real-money gaming carries genuine financial risk, is not a
        guaranteed or reliable source of income, and outcomes depend on a
        combination of skill and chance. Only play with money you can afford
        to lose. See our <a href="/responsible-gaming/">Responsible Gaming</a>
        page for more.
      </p>

      <h2>Jurisdiction and Legality</h2>
      <p>
        The legal status of real-money card games varies by country and, in
        India, by state, and can change over time. We do not make a
        blanket claim that Gold Rummy is legal, licensed or available
        everywhere. You are responsible for confirming whether real-money
        gaming is permitted in your specific location before creating an
        account or playing.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        This site may link to Gold Rummy's own app or to other external
        resources. We aren't responsible for the content, accuracy or
        practices of destinations outside our own domain.
      </p>

      <h2>Downloads</h2>
      <p>
        We encourage downloading the Gold Rummy APK only from a verified,
        official source, and we take reasonable care in how we present
        download information. We aren't responsible for files obtained from
        third-party mirrors, unofficial app stores, or links shared outside
        this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or corrections regarding this disclaimer can be sent
        through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }

  .text-sm.text-faint {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
